---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/docs.astro";
---

<DocsLayout title="Architecture — Querial">
    <div class="space-y-8">
        <div>
            <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-querial-indigo-on-dark">Start here</p>
            <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold mt-1">Architecture</h1>
        </div>
        <div class="prose dark:prose-invert max-w-none space-y-6 [&>p]:text-muted-foreground [&>h2]:text-foreground">
            <p>
                Querial is a control plane plus target-local execution. The browser never
                becomes the query engine. The control database never stores business rows
                from tenant pipelines.
            </p>
            <pre class="rounded-xl border border-border/50 bg-muted/40 p-4 text-sm overflow-x-auto"><code>Browser (MVC)
    → Platform API
    → PostgreSQL 18 + pgvector (control database)
    → Workers / registered agents
         → PostgreSQL | SQL Server | MySQL targets
         → optional S3-compatible artifact store
         → embedded DuckDB on eligible agents</code></pre>

            <h2>Control plane</h2>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1 text-muted-foreground">
                <li>Web UI: Tabler, collapsible left sidebar, no application-level top bar, no CDN UI libraries.</li>
                <li>Separate API host.</li>
                <li>Dapper-only persistence. Custom numbered SQL migrations.</li>
                <li>ASP.NET Core Identity with a Platform admin role. Project roles live in membership tables, not Identity.</li>
                <li>AES-256-GCM for connection endpoint secrets. API keys are SHA-256 hashed, shown once.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2>Execution dual-path</h2>
            <p>
                Feature flags keep legacy ordered serial execution until DAG execution
                and registered agents are enabled. Legacy ordered pipelines import as
                sequential edges. Dedicated worker is the default; in-process is optional
                for compact local hosts.
            </p>

            <h2>Optional pieces</h2>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1 text-muted-foreground">
                <li><strong class="text-foreground">Git</strong> — optional remotes and package publication. Never required to run pipelines.</li>
                <li><strong class="text-foreground">Messaging</strong> — optional. Never the large-data path. Parquet does not travel on the bus.</li>
                <li><strong class="text-foreground">DuckDB</strong> — embedded in eligible agents, not a separate cluster.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2>Not in the baseline</h2>
            <p>
                General-purpose workflow engines, file-oriented ETL suites, streaming,
                replication, visual no-code transforms, a hidden intermediate representation
                that rewrites business SQL, and product-specific reporting logic in the core.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>
</DocsLayout>
